            <ArticleTitle>Meckel's diverticulum masked by a long period of gastric symptoms--a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>413-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Meckel's diverticulum (MD) is the most frequent congenital abnormality of the small bowel and it is often difficult to diagnose. The authors report a case of a patient with long-term symptoms erroneously not related with MD disease and developing a diverticulum perforation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
